      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "The probability it will not rain on Saturday is $100\\%$ minus the probability it rains on Saturday, so the probability is $100\\% - 60\\% = 40\\%$.\n\nThe probability of not raining on Sunday is $100\\%$ minus the probability it rains on Sunday, so $100\\% - 25\\% = 75\\%$.\n\nThe probability of rain on both days is the probability of rain on Saturday multiplied by the probability of rain on Sunday, since the events are independent. $40\\% \\times 75\\% = 30\\%$. The probability it will rain on both days, expressed as a percent, is $\\boxed{30\\%}$.",
